    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="770b1c58-3434-5a81-9ff0-7eb20fd70a7b" activityNameId="ba581131-3bff-55a0-9eba-4a033de77245" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ventilator unit 6700 m3/h, modular, w. filter, without silencer</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ventilator unit 6700 m3/h, modular, w. filter, without silencer
Disposal of a ventilator unit for a air handling unit with 6700 m3/h nominal air flow rate (at 2 m/s air speed in cross section of air filter or heat exchanger). Reference value of inventory is 1 m3/h air flow. Specific component weight: 0.06 kg/(m3/h), total weight: 0.085 kg/(m3/h), including average components for controls, inverter and electric control cabinet, material for 20 filter replacements (once a year for 20 years lifetime). The ventilator of the air handling unit includes a frame construction, one radial belt drive fan, multi-leaf damper. No heat recovery, heating and/or cooling elements, humidifier, air-mixing plenum and silencer included. The frame construction made of aluminium-profiles, casing made of hot-dip galvanized and powder coated steel sheets insulated with polyurethane foam.;
UUID: 03622fc1-e009-45d1-b567-7fad089fccb3
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces, copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_03622fc1-e009-45d1-b567-7fad089fccb3.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
